{"questions":[{"question_id":"IAka2TsVobR0rDC5","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"heat-and-thermodynamics","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"specific-heat-capacity-calorimetry-and-change-of-state","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0.75,"permalink":"two-moles-of-ideal-helium-gas-are-in-a-rubber-balloon-at-30o-2012-marks-3-iaka2tsvobr0rdc5.htm","content":"Two moles of ideal helium gas are in a rubber balloon at 30<sup>o</sup>C. The balloon is fully expandable\nand can be assumed to require no energy in its expansion. The temperature of the gas in the balloon is slowly changed to 35<sup>o</sup>C. The amount of heat required in raising the temperature is\nnearly (take R = 8.31 J/mol.K)","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"62 J"},{"identifier":"B","content":"104 J"},{"identifier":"C","content":"124 J"},{"identifier":"D","content":"208 J"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<p>Here's a breakdown of how to solve this problem:</p>\n\n<p><strong>Understanding the Concepts</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ideal Gas:</strong> An ideal gas is a theoretical gas that follows the ideal gas law perfectly. The ideal gas law is a relationship between pressure (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.699ex\" height=\"1.545ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 751 683\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), volume (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.74ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 769 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), temperature (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.622ex\" height=\"1.532ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 717 677\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>), and the number of moles (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.357ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 600 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) of a gas:</li>\n</ul>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.05ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"11.153ex\" height=\"1.595ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 4929.6 705\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D443\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D443\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(751,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1797.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2853.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3453.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4212.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, where <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.048ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.717ex\" height=\"1.593ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 759 704\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is the ideal gas constant.</p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Heat Capacity:</strong>  Heat capacity is the amount of heat energy required to raise the temperature of a substance by 1 degree Celsius (or 1 Kelvin).  For an ideal gas, we can use the specific heat capacity at constant volume (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.357ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.581ex\" height=\"1.952ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1140.9 862.8\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) or at constant pressure (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.65ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.61ex\" height=\"2.245ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 1153.7 992.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>).</li><br>\n<li><strong>Constant Volume Process:</strong> In a constant volume process, the volume of the gas remains constant. The heat required to raise the temperature is given by:</li>\n</ul>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.252ex\" height=\"2.059ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 5415.5 910\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1068.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2124.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2724.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3865.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4698.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Constant Pressure Process:</strong> In a constant pressure process, the pressure of the gas remains constant. The heat required to raise the temperature is given by:</li>\n</ul>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.65ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.281ex\" height=\"2.27ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 5428.2 1003.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1068.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2124.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2724.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3878.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4711.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Molar Heat Capacities of Helium:</strong> Helium is a monatomic gas. For monatomic gases, we have:</li><br>\n<li><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.111ex\" height=\"2.736ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.2 4027.1 1209.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D463\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D463\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1418.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2474.5,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3268.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></li><br>\n<li><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"9.14ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 4039.8 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1431.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\" transform=\"translate(2487.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(220,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><rect width=\"553.6\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3280.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D445\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D445\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Solving the Problem</strong></p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Identify the Process:</strong> Since the balloon is fully expandable, the pressure remains constant. This is a constant pressure process.</li><br>\n<li><strong>Calculate the Heat:</strong>  Use the formula for heat at constant pressure:</li>\n</ol>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.65ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.281ex\" height=\"2.27ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 5428.2 1003.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D444\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D444\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1068.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2124.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2724.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(3878.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"394\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-394\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(4711.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Substitute the Values:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.452ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.651ex\" height=\"2.149ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 6033.6 950\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(877.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(1933.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(2433.6,0)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\"> moles</text></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></li><br>\n<li><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.781ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"30.595ex\" height=\"2.737ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -864.9 13522.9 1209.9\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate